A||||3||Adrift||Q's about starting a manual car with no breaks||||5||
Z||000000||Adrift||11-07-2001||05:21 PM||||After a few weeks I finally got my car started, and in jerked forward which scared me (my parents cars parked right in front of me) so I turned the engine off. The breaks on this car aren't functioning yet  (Including the emergency break). It's a manual car. What's the best way to ensure that this car doesn't drive forward once I start it? (and  No, I wasn't touching the Gas pedal)||||reg||5
Z||000001||cid_colada||11-07-2001||05:30 PM||||I would just put some bricks in front and behind the wheels, and make sure the car is in neutral.<P><BR>Black 84 SE||||reg||1
Z||000002||Old Lar||11-07-2001||05:31 PM||||If it is a manual, push the clutch in, shift into neutral.<P>A 1980's manual transmission car shouldn't start if the clutch isn't pushed in. With the clutch in, the car should't move.<P>While in neutral a car shouldn't move. Put a wheel chuck in front of the tire.<P>The only other advice is to learn how to drive a car with a manual trasmission.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||artherd||11-08-2001||11:45 PM||||A: Fix the brakes?<P>&lt;ducks&gt;<P>Best!<BR>Ben<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
